@* Plan A16 (pass 25): CC Reaction Fire in the DEFENDER's window on a moving vehicle's MP expenditure in their Location (D7.2, D7.21, A11.6). The page
   shows it to the DEFENDER's view and the adjudicator only, offers the DEFENDER units there that the view sees (ruling R23.1), keeps the choice, and
   proposes the attack. *@
<h4>CC Reaction Fire</h4>
<p class="muted" id="reaction-help">
    In the DEFENDER's window on the moving vehicle's MP expenditure in their Location, one unbroken, unpinned DEFENDER unit, alone or with a
    SMC, may attack it in CC as its Defensive First Fire, after a PAATC against an AFV unless exempt or already passed this phase; after an
    OVR, only once the OVR is resolved (D7.2, D7.21, A11.6). The vehicle does not attack back.
</p>
<div class="toolbar">
    <label>
        Attacker
        <select id="reaction-attacker" value="@Attacker" @onchange="@(args => OnAttacker.InvokeAsync(args.Value as string ?? string.Empty))">
            <option value="">choose</option>
            @foreach (var unit in Attackers)
            {
                <option value="@unit">@unit</option>
            }
        </select>
    </label>
    <label>
        With SMC
        <select id="reaction-leader" value="@Leader" @onchange="@(args => OnLeader.InvokeAsync(args.Value as string ?? string.Empty))">
            <option value="">none</option>
            @foreach (var unit in Leaders)
            {
                <option value="@unit">@unit</option>
            }
        </select>
    </label>
    <button id="propose-reaction" disabled="@(Attacker.Length == 0)" @onclick="@(() => OnPropose.InvokeAsync())">Propose: CC Reaction Fire at @Vehicle</button>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The moving vehicle.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string Vehicle { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>The DEFENDER units that may attack it.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public IReadOnlyList<string> Attackers { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>Those that are SMC, who may join the attacker.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public IReadOnlyList<string> Leaders { get; set; } = [];

    [Parameter]
    public string Attacker { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Parameter]
    public string Leader { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnAttacker { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnLeader { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnPropose { get; set; }
}
